  "body": [
    "The configuration reads as a liquidity-fuelled hedge against the dollar itself. Gold is up 8% this week and 16% over the month, bitcoin has jumped 22% in a week, and copper sits at a 52-week high, up 6% on the month — all while the dollar index has slipped 2.5% over the month. Crucially, gold is rallying with long yields still near the top of their range (the 10-year at 4.64%, 87% of its 52-week span) and a curve that has steepened 5 basis points over the month. Gold rising alongside high yields is not a flight to safety; it is markets pricing inflation and fiscal risk into a weakening currency.",
    "Bitcoin outrunning gold — up 4% in gold terms over the month — confirms this is risk appetite and liquidity, not fear. Copper at record highs says real demand is intact.",
    "The tensions: Brent has fallen 11% over the month, and the copper/gold ratio is down 8%. The oil slide looks supply-side rather than demand-driven, given copper's strength, so the inflation-hedge reading carries more weight than any growth-scare signal."
